      "id": 1,
      "text": "Sperryville’s name appears on an 1821 map by John Wood, marking its early recognition.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sperryville%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1820, Francis Thornton Jr. began selling small lots along Main Street, laying the groundwork for Sperryville’s commercial core.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sperryville%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s post office opened in 1840, anchoring it as a regional hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sperryville%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Sperryville Historic District, listed on the Virginia Landmarks Registry in 1982, showcases unadorned wooden homes from the 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
